{"name":"Ostrich Egg","hex":"#dcd0bb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ostrich","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large flightless bird of the order Struthioniformes.\nThe most widespread species of that order, known as the common ostrich (Struthio camelus).","The most widespread species of that order, known as the common ostrich (Struthio camelus)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ostrich"},{"term":"egg","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, reptiles, and other animals, often housing an embryo within a membrane or shell during its development.\n\n  The (usually) non-developing, edible egg (sense 1.1) of a domestic fowl such as a duck, goose, or, especially, chicken;  the contents of such an egg or eggs used as food.","An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, reptiles, and other animals, often housing an embryo within a membrane or shell during its development.\n\n  The (usually) non-developing, edible egg (sense 1.1) of a domestic fowl such as a duck, goose, or, especially, chicken;  the contents of such an egg or eggs used as food."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To throw (especially rotten) eggs (noun sense 1.1.1) at (someone or something).","To throw (especially rotten) eggs (noun sense 1.1.1) at (someone or something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/egg"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ostrich egg","blocks":[{"text":"The egg of the ostrich is the largest of any living bird. The shell has a long history of use by humans as a container and for decorative artwork, including beads. The eggs are edible but not commonly eaten."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Ostrich_eggs_in_a_nest_at_an_ostrich_farm%2C_South_Pasadena%2C_ca.1900_%28CHS-823%29.jpg/330px-Ostrich_eggs_in_a_nest_at_an_ostrich_farm%2C_South_Pasadena%2C_ca.1900_%28CHS-823%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ostrich_egg","wikidata":"Q28969642"},{"title":"Ostrich","blocks":[{"text":"Ostriches are large flightless birds. Two living species are recognised: the common ostrich, native to large parts of Sub-Saharan Africa, and the Somali ostrich, native to the Horn of Africa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Struthio_Diversity.jpg/330px-Struthio_Diversity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ostrich","wikidata":"Q2576337"},{"title":"Egg","blocks":[{"text":"An egg is an organic vessel grown by an animal to carry a possibly fertilized egg cell – a zygote. Within the vessel, an embryo is incubated until it has developed enough to survive on its own, at which point the animal hatches. Reproductive structures similar to the egg in other kingdoms are termed \"spores\", or in spermatophytes \"seeds\", or in gametophytes \"egg cells\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg/330px-Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egg","wikidata":"Q17147"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Vessel_of_ostrich_eggs_gold_copper_Mycenaean_1400_BC%2C_NAMA_7337_080864.jpg/120px-Vessel_of_ostrich_eggs_gold_copper_Mycenaean_1400_BC%2C_NAMA_7337_080864.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Vessel_of_ostrich_eggs_gold_copper_Mycenaean_1400_BC%2C_NAMA_7337_080864.jpg/250px-Vessel_of_ostrich_eggs_gold_copper_Mycenaean_1400_BC%2C_NAMA_7337_080864.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Vessel_of_ostrich_eggs_gold